```
#reason: The question asks for the first-level landcover type of the location with the highest average temperature in Thessaly Region on July 15, 2010. To answer this, we need to find the location (latitude, longitude) with the maximum tmean value from meteo_tmean on July 15, 2010, then join it with landcover_upscaled to get the ranks array, expand the ranks array to access landcover codes, and finally join with landcover_type to get the level1_label. The GEO_CONTEXT provides the valid latitude-longitude points in Thessaly Region, so we filter meteo_tmean and landcover_upscaled to only include coordinates within those points. Since landcover_upscaled.ranks is an ARRAY of arrays, we must UNNEST it to extract individual landcover codes and match them with landcover_type.
#columns: landcover_type.level1_label, meteo_tmean.tmean, meteo_tmean.latitude, meteo_tmean.longitude, landcover_upscaled.ranks
#values: 'July 15, 2010' refer to meteo_tmean.time = '2010-07-15 00:00:00', Thessaly Region refer to meteo_tmean.latitude IN (39.5, 39.6, 39.7, 39.4, 39.8, 39.2, 39.3, 39.9, 40.0, 39.1) AND meteo_tmean.longitude IN (21.2, 21.3, 21.4, 21.5, 21.6, 21.7, 21.8, 21.9, 22.0, 22.1, 22.2, 22.3, 22.4, 22.5, 22.6, 22.7, 22.8, 22.9, 23.0, 23.1, 23.2, 23.3, 23.4, 23.5, 23.6, 23.7, 23.8, 23.9, 24.0, 24.1, 24.2, 24.3, 24.4)
#SELECT: landcover_type.level1_label
#SQL: SELECT lt.level1_label
FROM meteo_tmean mt
JOIN landcover_upscaled lu ON mt.latitude = lu.latitude AND mt.longitude = lu.longitude
JOIN LATERAL UNNEST(lu.ranks) AS rank_array ON true
JOIN landcover_type lt ON lt.level3_code = rank_array[1][1]  -- Extract first code from nested array
WHERE mt.time = '2010-07-15 00:00:00'
  AND mt.latitude IN (39.5, 39.6, 39.7, 39.4, 39.8, 39.2, 39.3, 39.9, 40.0, 39.1)
  AND mt.longitude IN (21.2, 21.3, 21.4, 21.5, 21.6, 21.7, 21.8, 21.9, 22.0, 22.1, 22.2, 22.3, 22.4, 22.5, 22.6, 22.7, 22.8, 22.9, 23.0, 23.1, 23.2, 23.3, 23.4, 23.5, 23.6, 23.7, 23.8, 23.9, 24.0, 24.1, 24.2, 24.3, 24.4)
ORDER BY mt.tmean DESC
LIMIT 1;
```

