#reason: The question asks to compare the average annual temperatures between 2015 and 2020 for dominant forest and urban landcovers in the Canton of Zurich. The temperature data is stored in meteo_tmean.tmean (in Kelvin), and landcover information is in landcover_upscaled.ranks (array of landcover codes). We need to filter for the Canton of Zurich using the provided latitude/longitude points, extract the dominant landcover (first element of ranks array), join with landcover_type to filter for 'Forest and semi-natural areas' and 'Urban areas' (assuming 'Urban' is a level1_label not listed but implied by context), and compute average tmean per year (2015 and 2020). The ontology function describes a heatwave chain, but the question only asks for average annual temperature, so we ignore the heatwave logic and use only tmean with unit conversion (Kelvin to Celsius) as per the ontology's KelvinToCelsiusRule. We must UNNEST ranks to access landcover codes and join with landcover_type on level3 code (implied by schema note).
#columns: meteo_tmean.tmean, landcover_upscaled.ranks, landcover_type.level1_label, meteo_tmean.time
#values: 'Forest and semi-natural areas' refer to landcover_type.level1_label: 'Forest and semi-natural areas', 'Urban' refer to landcover_type.level1_label: 'Urban' (assumed), 2015 refer to EXTRACT(YEAR FROM meteo_tmean.time) = 2015, 2020 refer to EXTRACT(YEAR FROM meteo_tmean.time) = 2020, latitude between 47.2 and 47.6 refer to meteo_tmean.latitude BETWEEN 47.2 AND 47.6, longitude between 8.4 and 8.8 refer to meteo_tmean.longitude BETWEEN 8.4 AND 8.8
#SELECT: EXTRACT(YEAR FROM meteo_tmean.time), AVG(meteo_tmean.tmean - 273.15)
#SQL-like: Show EXTRACT(YEAR FROM meteo_tmean.time), AVG(meteo_tmean.tmean - 273.15), where condition is landcover_type.level1_label in ('Forest and semi-natural areas', 'Urban') and meteo_tmean.latitude between 47.2 and 47.6 and meteo_tmean.longitude between 8.4 and 8.8 and EXTRACT(YEAR FROM meteo_tmean.time) in (2015, 2020), Group by EXTRACT(YEAR FROM meteo_tmean.time)
#SQL: SELECT EXTRACT(YEAR FROM t.time) AS year, AVG(t.tmean - 273.15) AS avg_temp_celsius
FROM meteo_tmean t
JOIN (
    SELECT latitude, longitude, (UNNEST(ranks))[1][1] AS landcover_code
    FROM landcover_upscaled
    WHERE latitude BETWEEN 47.2 AND 47.6
      AND longitude BETWEEN 8.4 AND 8.8
) lc ON t.latitude = lc.latitude AND t.longitude = lc.longitude
JOIN landcover_type lt ON lc.landcover_code = lt.level3_code  -- assuming level3_code exists and maps to first element of ranks
WHERE lt.level1_label IN ('Forest and semi-natural areas', 'Urban')
  AND EXTRACT(YEAR FROM t.time) IN (2015, 2020)
GROUP BY EXTRACT(YEAR FROM t.time)
ORDER BY year;
```

